asn1c 18e56503 runtime, JER: the SEQUENCE decoder looks for each key from the
member after the last one decoded. A key naming an earlier member (members
out of ASN.1 order) is not found there and, in an extensible SEQUENCE, is
skipped as an unknown extension: the member is dropped without an error.
Our builders then lose an optional member written after its successor
(P2 Q5: E1AP PDCP-Configuration t-ReorderingTimer after discardTimer). The
decoder now refuses such a value. Row KS-PLAT-D10. Applied by
cmake/asn1c.cmake to a build-tree copy.

--- a/constr_SEQUENCE_jer.c
+++ b/constr_SEQUENCE_jer.c
@@ -265,6 +265,24 @@
                           edx, td->elements_count);
             }
 
+            /*
+             * A key that names a member before the one decoded last is a
+             * member out of order: the forward search above does not find
+             * it, and the extension skip below would drop it in silence.
+             * JSON object members are unordered (X.697), so this decoder,
+             * which reads them in ASN.1 order only, refuses the value.
+             */
+            {
+                size_t m;
+                for(m = 0; m < td->elements_count && m < (size_t)edx; m++) {
+                    if(jer_check_sym(ptr, ch_size, td->elements[m].name) == JCK_KEY) {
+                        ASN_DEBUG("JER/SEQUENCE: member %s out of ASN.1 order",
+                                  td->elements[m].name);
+                        RETURN(RC_FAIL);
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+
             /* It is expected extension */
             if(IN_EXTENSION_GROUP(specs,
                 edx + (edx < td->elements_count
